<h1>Cisco Secure AI Tokens Commercial Framework (Dual Procurement Paths)</h1>

<p>Framework for enterprise and neocloud motions: direct Cisco procurement through Solutions+ / GPL, or direct platform activation with quarterly/half-year partner settlement.</p>

<p>Equinix already has both selling motions in place today: enterprise-led Cisco procurement and platform-led activation with reconciliation. This model adapts that framework for Cisco Secure AI Tokens.</p>

<p class="strip">Enterprise Seller Motion &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; Neocloud Platform Motion &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; BYOL Support &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; Merchant of Record &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; Q / H Partner Settlement</p>

<h2>Path A — Enterprise-Led Procurement (Cisco Direct Motion)</h2>

<p>Enterprise account sellers position and sell Cisco Secure AI Tokens through Solutions+ / GPL, attach Cisco SD-WAN HW/SW and Galileo, and support BYOL portability into target neocloud and frontier environments (Diamond Tier).</p>

<ol>
    <li>Cisco AE identifies AI/Neocloud use case and proposes reference architecture.</li>
    <li>Enterprise procures Cisco Secure AI Tokens via Solutions+ / GPL and selects Cisco SD-WAN/Security components.</li>
    <li>Cisco SD-WAN HW/SW deployed; policy, segmentation, and Galileo configured for Neocloud/Frontier access.</li>
    <li>BYOL enabled: enterprise can apply existing eligible Cisco licenses to supported deployments.</li>
    <li>Enterprise consumes inference services (Diamond Tier: OpenAI / Anthropic Claude, plus Platinum/Gold) with Cisco-led commercial attribution at sale.</li>
</ol>

<p><strong>Enterprise Buying Programs (Micro Segment):</strong> Align procurement to existing buying constructs to simplify approvals and expand attach.</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>EA’s:</strong> Use enterprise agreement structures for predictable token consumption.</li>
    <li><strong>WPAS:</strong> Use approved buying pathways to streamline Secure AI Tokens + SD-WAN acquisition cycles.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Path B — Neocloud/Platform Direct Activation (Settlement Motion)</h2>

<p>End customer activates Cisco Secure AI Tokens directly within Neocloud/inferencing marketplaces, including partners such as Qumulus, Cirrascale, and Massed Compute (Platinum and Gold Tiers).</p>

<ol>
    <li>Customer signs up with Neocloud provider (e.g., Qumulus, Cirrascale, Massed Compute).</li>
    <li>Customer enables Cisco Secure AI Token consumption from provider catalog.</li>
    <li>BYOL option: customer brings eligible existing Cisco licenses where supported by the platform model.</li>
    <li>Usage/subscription data is mapped to eligible token and model attribution rules.</li>
    <li>Cisco acts as Merchant of Record and executes partner settlement (compensating the model builder and neocloud) at end of quarter or half-year per partner agreement.</li>
</ol>

