<h2>End-User POV and Business Implications</h2>

<p>Most end customers care about speed, price, performance, and support outcomes—not internal route mechanics. If experience is equivalent, Cisco should prioritize the motion that maximizes attach and efficiency.</p>

<p><strong>Path A:</strong> Familiar enterprise procurement model, centralized sourcing controls, programmatic buying (EA/WPAS), and direct access to top-tier Diamond models (OpenAI/Anthropic).</p>

<p><strong>Path B:</strong> Fast in-platform activation through neocloud ecosystems (Qumulus, Cirrascale, Massed Compute), plus BYOL flexibility where supported.</p>

<p><strong>Why both benefit Cisco:</strong> Neocloud route enables direct sell-through with partner settlement; enterprise route drives Tokens and SDCI via Solutions+ / GPL and keeps AEs incented.</p>

<p><strong>Incentive alignment:</strong> Enterprise AEs are motivated to push business to neoclouds because token and attribution models maintain compensation linkage.</p>

